---
/**
 * Footer — the site footer.
 *
 * Recreates design/README.md §9 (Footer) and the approved reference in
 * design/design-reference/Basset Landing.dc.html exactly: a full-bleed
 * white surface with a 1px hairline top border carrying the site's single
 * collaboration credit — "Basset, a collaboration between Snapp Automotive
 * and [mugo-mark] mugo works". Mono 13px muted, links use the accent-text
 * green with the accent-hover on hover. No email address per the brief
 * (client decision).
 *
 * Structure mirrors the reference exactly: the mugo mark sits inside the
 * mugo works anchor (not outside it), so the mark and its label stay a
 * single clickable unit and — with white-space: nowrap on the link — never
 * split across a line break. The mark is the same verbatim asset the Nav
 * uses (public/mugo-mark.svg), served at 15x15 here per the brief's §9
 * (the Nav uses it at 18x18 per §1); QA verifies the asset is not
 * recoloured.
 *
 * The footer sits outside .content in src/pages/index.astro so its top
 * hairline reaches the viewport edges, mirroring the Nav's structure at
 * the top of the page. Internal padding uses --content-padding-x so the
 * text's inner edges line up with the content column above it.
 *
 * Every color, size, spacing, and copy string here is bound by the brief;
 * values live in src/styles/tokens.css and are read through the token
 * custom properties. QA verifies against design/README.md §9 at 1440x900
 * and 390x844.
 */
---

<footer class="footer">
  Basset, a collaboration between
  <a
    class="external-link"
    href="https://www.snappautomotive.io"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener"
  >Snapp Automotive</a>
  and
  <a
    class="external-link mugo-link"
    href="https://www.mugoworks.com"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener"
  ><img
      class="mugo-mark"
      src="/mugo-mark.svg"
      alt=""
      width="15"
      height="15"
    />mugo works</a>
</footer>

<style>
  /* Container — full-bleed white bar with the 1px hairline top border the
     brief specifies. Internal padding uses --content-padding-x so the
     footer's inner edges line up with the .content column above it. Mono
     13px muted per the brief's §9 typography row. Left-aligned within the
     same content width as the reference. */
  .footer {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
    padding: 22px var(--content-padding-x);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-footer);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  /* External-link — the two links share the same accent-text green with
     the accent-hover on hover per the brief. text-decoration is off to
     match the reference; the :focus-visible outline provides the visible
     keyboard affordance the brief's a11y clause requires. border-radius
     on the outline gives a cleaner rectangular ring around the anchor's
     text box. */
  .external-link {
    color: var(--color-accent-text);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .external-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-link-hover);
  }

  .external-link:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent-text);
    outline-offset: 2px;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  /* mugo-link — the mugo works anchor contains the inline mark plus the
     label text. white-space: nowrap keeps the mark and "mugo works" on
     one line at every viewport width so the mark never orphans onto its
     own line above the label. */
  .mugo-link {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* mugo mark — 15x15 verbatim asset (smaller than the nav's 18x18 per the
     brief's §9). vertical-align: -3px matches the reference's baseline
     nudge so the mark sits centred on the mono text's x-height; the 4px
     right margin gives the small breathing gap between the mark and
     "mugo works" the reference specifies. Width/height attributes on the
     <img> reserve the box; this rule pins the box explicitly so a stray
     global img rule cannot resize it. */
  .mugo-mark {
    width: 15px;
    height: 15px;
    vertical-align: -3px;
    margin-right: 4px;
  }
</style>
